  "findings": [
    "All sixteen current composition captures were re-rendered after requirement-allocation updates and remain byte-identical to the preceding inspected revision. Source records changed; scene geometry and placements did not.",
    "The station, guys, cart and independent solar/ambient instruments remain visible in the same outdoor area. The ground is an authored earth/footing/walkway design, not a reconstructed paper roof.",
    "Ordinary trays remain supported on the same cart. Three source-sized drivers, a wire-rope cutter, an adjustable wrench, a tape measure, an engineer hammer, two assigned spatulas, two independent grease tubes and one 300-wipe pack occupy distinct service-worktop locations. The spatulas retain neutral-roll references without dynamic stability credit.",
    "The broad station view retains buried geometry in its fit bounds; close instrument details remain available through the linked station inspector.",
    "The two remaining wire spirals and seventeen unused kit mesh parts occupy the actual cart lower shelf and a third ordinary tray. Their source lengths, exact kit surfaces, physical support and all eleven existing installed humanoid pose witnesses were checked independently.",
    "The new cutter retains the isolated inspector geometry without duplication. Its detailed source and joint inspector is linked from the inventory-owner table. Browser bounds use transformed vertices for the slightly tilted tool, not rotated local boxes.",
    "The Crescent candidate remains one shared identity in all alternative service views. Its source, both scales, internal guide and actual outer-nut fits are linked from the inventory table. The staged reference retains at least 2.35 mm inferred mass-centre support margin.",
    "One Super Lube 21030 tube rests upright on its actual cap base at the service worktop, clear of tools and complete surrounding geometry. Container and nominal 85 g stock share one identity. Its inspector is linked from the identity table; U30 silicone grease is represented by a separate 93003 candidate; its application remains unqualified.",
    "The closed Hultafors BT5M rests on its actual case base, with the full clip and hook inside the service worktop and clear of surrounding actual geometry. One case, blade and clip share one selected identity across all inspection shapes. Its source and scale inspector is linked from the identity table.",
    "The Stanley 56-204 candidate rests on actual head and handle contacts at the front of the service worktop. Its initially rejected rear position intersected the retained ambient RTD lead; that placement is preserved as a negative case in the composition checks. The probe and cable remain present.",
    "One 93003 silicone-grease tube rests on its cap base at the service bench, clear of the retained RTD, cable and solar sensor. It shares one nominal 85 g inventory across both density scenarios and is linked to its separate inspector.",
    "The two visually identical spatulas retain distinct lubricant assignments and are linked to their common source inspector. The single TX609 pack preserves all 300 contained wipe identities and both packaging films. Current actual-geometry checks preserve hollow film cavities and clear the retained ambient RTD lead and independent solar sensor."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Base versus installed is a reviewer state switch, not an executed assembly or transfer.",
    "The base model count, original floorplan and original 94 workspace poses remain explicitly separated from the composed installed reference.",
    "Complete initial stock, omitted preparation components and the removal/cut disposition of the two temporary mast ties still require reconciliation.",
    "No new geometry, material, force, safety or owner acceptance is implied by these captures."
